/-!
# Closure properties of finitely generated groups

Mathlib has a substantial theory of finitely generated commutative groups in
`Mathlib/GroupTheory/FiniteAbelian/Basic.lean` — the structure theorem,
`finite_of_fg_isMulTorsion`, and
`Subgroup.finiteIndex_range_powMonoidHom_of_fg`, which is the finiteness of `G ⧸ Gⁿ`. Three
closure properties it does not carry are collected here, together with finiteness of the torsion
subgroup, a `Fin`-indexed form of finite generation, surjective presentations of finitely
generated abelian groups from finite powers of `ℤ`, and the choice of finitely many generators
from any generating set.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CommGroup.finite_torsion_of_fg` and `TauCeti.AddCommGroup.finite_torsion_of_fg`: the
  torsion subgroup of a finitely generated abelian group is finite, using Mathlib's
  `CommGroup.finite_of_fg_isMulTorsion`.
* `TauCeti.CommGroup.exists_finiteIndex_isMulTorsionFree` and
  `TauCeti.AddCommGroup.exists_finiteIndex_isAddTorsionFree`: a finitely generated abelian group
  has a torsion-free subgroup of finite index.
* `TauCeti.CommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_zpowersPiHom_surjective`,
  `TauCeti.AddCommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_zmultiplesPiHom_surjective`,
  `TauCeti.CommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_monoidHom_surjective`, and
  `TauCeti.AddCommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_addMonoidHom_surjective`: a commutative group is finitely
  generated exactly when it admits a surjective homomorphism from a finite power of `ℤ`.

* `AddSubgroup.fg_of_addCommGroup` and `Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup`: a subgroup of a finitely
  generated commutative group is finitely generated. The argument is Noetherianity of `ℤ`, so the
  *additive* statement is the foundational one and the multiplicative statement is transported
  from it through `Additive`; `to_additive` cannot relate them — it would have to translate the
  `ℤ`-module argument itself — so the pair is written out by hand and registered with
  `to_additive existing`. Both are `instance`s, matching how Mathlib states its other `FG` closure
  properties (`Group.fg_range`, `QuotientGroup.fg`, `Subgroup.fg_of_index_ne_zero`).
* `Subgroup.FG.of_le` and `AddSubgroup.FG.of_le`: the relative form, a subgroup of a finitely
  generated subgroup of a commutative group is finitely generated.
* `IsMulFG.ulift` and `IsAddFG.ulift`: universe lifts preserve finite generation.
* `IsMulFG.finite_monoidHom` and `IsAddFG.finite_addMonoidHom`: there are finitely many
  homomorphisms from a finitely generated unital magma (for instance a finitely generated monoid
  or group) to a finite one.
* `Group.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family`: a group is finitely generated exactly when it
  is generated by a tuple indexed by some `Fin n`, the form in which marked groups record their
  generators.
* `Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`: a subgroup `K` whose image `K.map φ` and whose
  intersection `K ⊓ φ.ker` with the kernel are finitely generated is itself finitely generated.
  This is the `Subgroup` analogue of Mathlib's `Submodule.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`, an absence
  Mathlib records explicitly — a comment in
  `Mathlib/NumberTheory/NumberField/Units/DirichletTheorem.lean` restructures a proof "due to no
  `Subgroup` version of `Submodule.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker` existing". It carries the generator
  argument, and needs no commutativity.
* `Group.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range`: an extension of finitely generated groups is finitely
  generated — if the kernel and the range of `φ : G →* H` are finitely generated then so is `G`.
  It is the `K = ⊤` case of `Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`, and is derived from it. It is
  a plain theorem rather than an instance, because `φ` is an explicit argument that typeclass
  resolution cannot infer.
* `Subgroup.FG.exists_finite_subset_le_closure`: a finitely generated subgroup contained in the
  subgroup generated by a set `S` is contained in the subgroup generated by a finite subset of `S`,
  the `Subgroup` analogue of Mathlib's `Submodule.subset_span_finite_of_subset_span`.
* `Subgroup.FG.exists_pow_mem_of_mem_of_pow_mem`: for a finitely generated subgroup `H` of a
  commutative group and any subgroup `E`, one exponent `u ≠ 0` sends every element of `H` with a
  nonzero power in `E` into `E`, because the torsion of `H ⧸ (E ⊓ H)` is finite.

`Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker` and `Group.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range` are both
`@[to_additive]`, and both are steps towards the `S`-unit group being finitely generated, an input
to the weak Mordell–Weil theorem: the group of `S`-units sits in an extension whose kernel is the
unit group of the base and whose range is a subgroup of a free group of rank `|S|`, so establishing
finite generation needs exactly these two facts. The finiteness that the descent then applies to it
is Mathlib's `Subgroup.finiteIndex_range_powMonoidHom_of_fg`, read through
`Subgroup.finiteIndex_iff_finite_quotient`; nothing here reproves it.

`AddSubgroup.fg_of_addCommGroup`, `Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup` and `Group.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range`
are adapted from Michael Stoll's elliptic-curves formalisation
(`github.com/MichaelStollBayreuth/EllipticCurves`, `EllipticCurves/Mathlib/SelmerGroup.lean` at
commit `66889eada51a`, Apache 2.0, by Michael Stoll). Following this repository's convention for
adapted material, the upstream authorship is credited here rather than in the copyright header.

**`Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker` is new here**, with no counterpart in that source, which
has only the `K = ⊤` case; Mathlib records the general statement's absence in the comment at
`Mathlib/NumberTheory/NumberField/Units/DirichletTheorem.lean` quoted above. The generator
argument is Stoll's, restated for a subgroup.

That source file also carries `finite_modPow`, `finite_of_fg_of_pow_eq_one` and two `ℤ`-module
translation helpers. **None of them is ported: all four are now in Mathlib** — as
`Subgroup.finiteIndex_range_powMonoidHom_of_fg`, `CommGroup.finite_of_fg_isMulTorsion`, the
instance `AddMonoid.FG.to_moduleFinite_int`, and `Module.Finite.iff_addGroup_fg` composed with
`AddGroup.fg_iff_mul_fg`. The source predates those additions, some of which its own author
upstreamed, so check Mathlib again before porting anything further from it.

**Concurrent work upstream.** The open Mathlib pull request
[mathlib4#40791](https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40791) ("dirichlet's s-unit
theorem", by `vvvv-ops`, open since 2026-06-19) carries two of the results here as file-local
helpers of `Mathlib/RingTheory/DedekindDomain/SUnit.lean`, under different names:
`Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup` as `Subgroup.fg_of_fg_commGroup`, and
`Group.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range` as `CommGroup.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range` — the latter
`CommGroup`-only, where the version here needs no commutativity. On a bump that lands #40791, drop
`Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup` in favour of upstream's; the extension lemma here is strictly more
general, and `Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker` has no counterpart there at all.
-/

public section

/-- **A subgroup of a finitely generated additive commutative group is finitely generated.** The
additive form of `Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup`. -/
-- `ℤ` is Noetherian, so `G` is a finitely generated `ℤ`-module and hence Noetherian, and the
-- submodule corresponding to `H` is finitely generated. The argument is about `ℤ`-modules, which
-- is why this additive form is the one proved directly.
instance (priority := 100) AddSubgroup.fg_of_addCommGroup {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G]
    [AddGroup.FG G] (H : AddSubgroup G) : AddGroup.FG H :=
  (AddGroup.fg_iff_addSubgroup_fg H).mpr <| H.toIntSubmodule_toAddSubgroup ▸
    (Submodule.fg_iff_addSubgroup_fg _).mp (IsNoetherian.noetherian (R := ℤ) H.toIntSubmodule)

/-- **A subgroup of a finitely generated commutative group is finitely generated.** The
multiplicative form of `AddSubgroup.fg_of_addCommGroup`. -/
-- Transported through `Additive G`. `to_additive` cannot relate the two — it would have to
-- translate the `ℤ`-module argument itself — so the pair is written out by hand and registered
-- with `to_additive existing`, which puts it in the dictionary so downstream `@[to_additive]`
-- proofs using either can translate.
@[to_additive existing]
instance (priority := 100) Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup {G : Type*} [CommGroup G] [Group.FG G]
    (H : Subgroup G) : Group.FG H :=
  -- `AddGroup.FG (Additive G)` is Mathlib's instance `AddGroup.fg_of_group_fg`, found by search
  (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg H).mpr <| (Subgroup.fg_iff_add_fg H).mpr <|
    (AddGroup.fg_iff_addSubgroup_fg (Subgroup.toAddSubgroup H)).mp inferInstance

/-- **A subgroup of a finitely generated subgroup of a commutative group is finitely generated.**
The relative form of `Subgroup.fg_of_commGroup`, the analogue of Mathlib's `Submodule.FG.of_le`
over a Noetherian ring. -/
@[to_additive /-- **An additive subgroup of a finitely generated additive subgroup of an additive
commutative group is finitely generated.** The relative form of `AddSubgroup.fg_of_addCommGroup`.
-/]
theorem Subgroup.FG.of_le {G : Type*} [CommGroup G] {H K : Subgroup G} (hK : K.FG) (h : H ≤ K) :
    H.FG :=
  have : Group.FG K := (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg K).mpr hK
  (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg H).mp <| Group.fg_of_surjective
    (f := (H.subgroupOfEquivOfLe h).toMonoidHom) (H.subgroupOfEquivOfLe h).surjective

/-- **A subgroup whose image and whose intersection with the kernel are finitely generated is
itself finitely generated.** The `Subgroup` analogue of Mathlib's
`Submodule.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`, whose absence Mathlib records explicitly: a comment in
`Mathlib/NumberTheory/NumberField/Units/DirichletTheorem.lean` restructures a proof "due to no
`Subgroup` version of `Submodule.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker` existing".

`Group.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range` is its `K = ⊤` case. -/
-- `K` is generated by preimages in `K` of generators of `K.map φ`, together with generators of
-- `K ⊓ φ.ker`: an `x ∈ K` agrees under `φ` with some `n` in their closure `N`, and then `n⁻¹ * x`
-- lies in `K ⊓ φ.ker ≤ N`.
@[to_additive /-- **An additive subgroup whose image and whose intersection with the kernel are
finitely generated is itself finitely generated.** The `AddSubgroup` analogue of Mathlib's
`Submodule.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`. `AddGroup.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range` is its `K = ⊤`
case. -/]
theorem Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker {G H : Type*} [Group G] [Group H] (φ : G →* H)
    {K : Subgroup G} (h₁ : (K.map φ).FG) (h₂ : (K ⊓ φ.ker).FG) : K.FG := by
  obtain ⟨T, hT, hTfin⟩ := (Subgroup.fg_iff _).mp h₁
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hSfin⟩ := (Subgroup.fg_iff _).mp h₂
  -- a preimage in `K` for each generator of the image
  have hTmem : ∀ t ∈ T, ∃ g, g ∈ K ∧ φ g = t := fun t ht ↦
    Subgroup.mem_map.mp (by rw [← hT]; exact Subgroup.subset_closure ht)
  choose! σ hσK hσ using hTmem
  have hSle : S ⊆ (K ⊓ φ.ker : Subgroup G) := by rw [← hS]; exact Subgroup.subset_closure
  refine (Subgroup.fg_iff _).mpr ⟨σ '' T ∪ S, ?_, (hTfin.image σ).union hSfin⟩
  set N := Subgroup.closure (σ '' T ∪ S) with hN
  -- the generators lie in `K`
  have hle : N ≤ K := by
    rw [hN, Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro g (⟨t, ht, rfl⟩ | hg)
    exacts [hσK t ht, (hSle hg).1]
  refine le_antisymm hle fun x hx ↦ ?_
  -- `φ x` is hit by `N`, since `N.map φ` contains every generator of `K.map φ`
  have hTle : T ⊆ (N.map φ : Set H) := fun t ht ↦
    ⟨σ t, Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_left _ ⟨t, ht, rfl⟩), hσ t ht⟩
  have hxT : φ x ∈ Subgroup.closure T := by rw [hT]; exact ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨n, hnN, hn⟩ := (Subgroup.closure_le _).mpr hTle hxT
  -- so `n⁻¹ * x` lies in `K ⊓ φ.ker`, hence in `N`
  have hker : n⁻¹ * x ∈ K ⊓ φ.ker :=
    ⟨K.mul_mem (K.inv_mem (hle hnN)) hx, by simp [hn]⟩
  rw [← hS] at hker
  have := (Subgroup.closure_le N).mpr
    (fun s hs ↦ Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_right _ hs)) hker
  simpa using N.mul_mem hnN this

/-- **An extension of finitely generated groups is finitely generated:** if the kernel and the
range of `φ : G →* H` are finitely generated, then so is `G`. This is the `K = ⊤` case of
`Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`. -/
@[to_additive /-- **An extension of finitely generated additive groups is finitely generated:** if
the kernel and the range of `φ : G →+ H` are finitely generated, then so is `G`. This is the
`K = ⊤` case of `AddSubgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker`. -/]
theorem Group.fg_of_fg_ker_of_fg_range {G H : Type*} [Group G] [Group H] (φ : G →* H)
    [Group.FG φ.ker] [Group.FG φ.range] : Group.FG G := by
  have h₁ : ((⊤ : Subgroup G).map φ).FG := by
    rw [← MonoidHom.range_eq_map]
    exact (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg _).mp ‹Group.FG φ.range›
  have h₂ : ((⊤ : Subgroup G) ⊓ φ.ker).FG := by
    rw [top_inf_eq]
    exact (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg _).mp ‹Group.FG φ.ker›
  -- `Group.FG G` is finite generation of `(⊤ : Subgroup G)`
  exact Group.fg_def.mpr (Subgroup.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker φ h₁ h₂)

/-- **A finitely generated subgroup inside the subgroup generated by a set is inside the subgroup
generated by a finite part of the set.** The `Subgroup` analogue of Mathlib's
`Submodule.subset_span_finite_of_subset_span`. -/
@[to_additive /-- **A finitely generated additive subgroup inside the additive subgroup generated
by a set is inside the additive subgroup generated by a finite part of the set.** The
`AddSubgroup` analogue of Mathlib's `Submodule.subset_span_finite_of_subset_span`. -/]
theorem Subgroup.FG.exists_finite_subset_le_closure {G : Type*} [Group G] {H : Subgroup G}
    (hH : H.FG) {S : Set G} (hS : H ≤ Subgroup.closure S) :
    ∃ T ⊆ S, T.Finite ∧ H ≤ Subgroup.closure T := by
  -- Every element generated by `S` is generated by a finite part of `S`.
  have key (g : G) (hg : g ∈ Subgroup.closure S) :
      ∃ T ⊆ S, T.Finite ∧ g ∈ Subgroup.closure T := by
    induction hg using Subgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem x hx => exact ⟨{x}, Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hx, Set.finite_singleton x,
        Subgroup.subset_closure rfl⟩
    | one => exact ⟨∅, Set.empty_subset S, Set.finite_empty, one_mem _⟩
    | mul x y _ _ hx hy =>
      obtain ⟨T₁, hT₁, hf₁, hx⟩ := hx
      obtain ⟨T₂, hT₂, hf₂, hy⟩ := hy
      exact ⟨T₁ ∪ T₂, Set.union_subset hT₁ hT₂, hf₁.union hf₂,
        mul_mem (Subgroup.closure_mono Set.subset_union_left hx)
          (Subgroup.closure_mono Set.subset_union_right hy)⟩
    | inv x _ hx =>
      obtain ⟨T, hT, hf, hx⟩ := hx
      exact ⟨T, hT, hf, inv_mem hx⟩
  obtain ⟨A, rfl, hA⟩ := (Subgroup.fg_iff _).mp hH
  choose! T hTS hTf hT using fun a (ha : a ∈ A) => key a (hS (Subgroup.subset_closure ha))
  exact ⟨⋃ a ∈ A, T a, Set.iUnion₂_subset hTS, hA.biUnion hTf, Subgroup.closure_le _ |>.mpr
    fun a ha => Subgroup.closure_mono (Set.subset_biUnion_of_mem ha) (hT a ha)⟩

/-- A group is finitely generated if and only if it is generated by a tuple indexed by some
`Fin n`. -/
@[to_additive /-- An additive group is finitely generated if and only if it is generated by a
tuple indexed by some `Fin n`. -/]
theorem Group.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family {G : Type*} [Group G] :
    Group.FG G ↔ ∃ (n : ℕ) (S : Fin n → G), Subgroup.closure (Set.range S) = ⊤ := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun ⟨n, S, hS⟩ => Group.fg_iff.2 ⟨_, hS, Set.finite_range S⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨n, s, rfl, hs⟩ := Group.fg_iff'.1 h
  exact ⟨_, Subtype.val ∘ s.equivFin.symm, by simpa using hs⟩

/-- A universe lift of a finitely generated magma is finitely generated. -/
@[to_additive /-- A universe lift of a finitely generated additive magma is finitely
generated. -/]
instance IsMulFG.ulift {M : Type*} [Mul M] [IsMulFG M] : IsMulFG (ULift M) :=
  (isMulFG_congr MulEquiv.ulift).mpr ‹_›

/-- There are finitely many monoid homomorphisms from a finitely generated unital magma to a
finite one, since a homomorphism is determined by its values on a finite generating set. -/
@[to_additive /-- There are finitely many additive monoid homomorphisms from a finitely generated
additive unital magma to a finite one, since a homomorphism is determined by its values on a
finite generating set. -/]
instance IsMulFG.finite_monoidHom {M N : Type*} [MulOneClass M] [IsMulFG M] [MulOneClass N]
    [Finite N] : Finite (M →* N) := by
  obtain ⟨S, hSfin, hS⟩ := Monoid.exists_finite_of_isMulFG M
  have := hSfin.to_subtype
  refine Finite.of_injective (fun f : M →* N => fun s : S => f s) fun f g hfg => ?_
  exact MonoidHom.eq_of_eqOn_denseM hS fun s hs => congr_fun hfg ⟨s, hs⟩

namespace TauCeti

/-- The torsion subgroup of a finitely generated abelian group is finite. -/
@[to_additive TauCeti.AddCommGroup.finite_torsion_of_fg
  /-- The torsion subgroup of a finitely generated additive abelian group is finite. -/]
theorem CommGroup.finite_torsion_of_fg (G : Type*) [CommGroup G] [Group.FG G] :
    Finite (_root_.CommGroup.torsion G) :=
  _root_.CommGroup.finite_of_fg_isMulTorsion _ fun P ↦
    (_root_.CommGroup.torsion G).subtype_injective.isOfFinOrder_iff.mp P.property

/-- A finitely generated abelian group has a torsion-free subgroup of finite index, namely the
subgroup of `n`-th powers, where `n` is the order of the torsion subgroup. -/
@[to_additive TauCeti.AddCommGroup.exists_finiteIndex_isAddTorsionFree
  /-- A finitely generated additive abelian group has a torsion-free subgroup of finite index,
  namely the subgroup of `n`-th multiples, where `n` is the order of the torsion subgroup. -/]
theorem CommGroup.exists_finiteIndex_isMulTorsionFree (G : Type*) [CommGroup G] [Group.FG G] :
    ∃ K : Subgroup G, K.FiniteIndex ∧ IsMulTorsionFree K := by
  have := CommGroup.finite_torsion_of_fg G
  let n := Nat.card (_root_.CommGroup.torsion G)
  refine ⟨(powMonoidHom n).range, Subgroup.finiteIndex_range_powMonoidHom_of_fg G Nat.card_pos.ne',
    .of_not_isOfFinOrder ?_⟩
  intro x hx hfin
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := x.property
  -- `x = g ^ n` has finite order, so `g` is torsion and its `n`-th power is trivial
  have hgn : IsOfFinOrder (g ^ n) := by
    simpa [← hg] using Submonoid.isOfFinOrder_coe.2 hfin
  have hg' : g ∈ _root_.CommGroup.torsion G :=
    (isOfFinOrder_pow.1 hgn).resolve_right Nat.card_pos.ne'
  refine hx (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [← hg]
  exact congrArg Subtype.val (pow_card_eq_one' (x := (⟨g, hg'⟩ : _root_.CommGroup.torsion G)))

/-- A commutative group is finitely generated if and only if it is the image of `zpowersPiHom` for
some `Fin n`-indexed tuple of generators. -/
theorem CommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_zpowersPiHom_surjective {G : Type*} [CommGroup G] :
    Group.FG G ↔
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (τ : Fin n → G),
        Function.Surjective (zpowersPiHom τ fun _ _ => .all _ _) := by
  rw [Group.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family]
  exact exists_congr fun n => exists_congr fun τ => (zpowersPiHom_surjective _ _).symm

/-- An additive commutative group is finitely generated if and only if it is the image of
`zmultiplesPiHom` for some `Fin n`-indexed tuple of generators. -/
theorem AddCommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_zmultiplesPiHom_surjective {A : Type*} [AddCommGroup A] :
    AddGroup.FG A ↔
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (τ : Fin n → A),
        Function.Surjective (zmultiplesPiHom τ fun _ _ => .all _ _) := by
  rw [AddGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family]
  exact exists_congr fun n => exists_congr fun τ => (zmultiplesPiHom_surjective _ _).symm

/-- An additive commutative group is finitely generated if and only if it admits a surjective
homomorphism from `Fin n → ℤ` for some `n : ℕ`. -/
theorem AddCommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_addMonoidHom_surjective {A : Type*} [AddCommGroup A] :
    AddGroup.FG A ↔ ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : (Fin n → ℤ) →+ A), Function.Surjective f := by
  rw [AddGroup.fg_def, AddSubgroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_addMonoidHom]
  exact exists_congr fun _ => exists_congr fun _ => AddMonoidHom.range_eq_top

/-- A commutative group is finitely generated if and only if it admits a surjective homomorphism
from `Fin n → Multiplicative ℤ` for some `n : ℕ`. -/
theorem CommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_monoidHom_surjective {G : Type*} [CommGroup G] :
    Group.FG G ↔ ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : (Fin n → Multiplicative ℤ) →* G), Function.Surjective f := by
  rw [GroupFG.iff_add_fg, AddCommGroup.fg_iff_exists_fin_addMonoidHom_surjective]
  refine exists_congr fun n => ⟨fun ⟨f, hf⟩ => ?_, fun ⟨f, hf⟩ => ?_⟩
  · refine ⟨f.toMultiplicativeLeft.comp (MulEquiv.funMultiplicative (Fin n) ℤ).symm.toMonoidHom, ?_⟩
    exact (Additive.toMul.surjective.comp (hf.comp Multiplicative.toAdd.surjective)).comp
      (MulEquiv.funMultiplicative (Fin n) ℤ).symm.surjective
  · refine ⟨(f.comp (MulEquiv.funMultiplicative (Fin n) ℤ).toMonoidHom).toAdditiveRight, ?_⟩
    exact Additive.ofMul.surjective.comp
      ((hf.comp (MulEquiv.funMultiplicative (Fin n) ℤ).surjective).comp
        Multiplicative.ofAdd.surjective)

end TauCeti

/-- **One exponent brings every root of `E` inside a finitely generated subgroup back to `E`.**
If `H` is a finitely generated subgroup of a commutative group and `E` is any subgroup, there is a
single `u ≠ 0` such that `y ^ u ∈ E` for every `y ∈ H` having some nonzero power in `E`. One can
take `u` to be the exponent of the torsion subgroup of `H ⧸ (E ⊓ H)`, which is finite. -/
@[to_additive /-- **One multiplier brings every root of `E` inside a finitely generated additive
subgroup back to `E`.** If `H` is a finitely generated additive subgroup of an additive commutative
group and `E` is any additive subgroup, there is a single `u ≠ 0` such that `u • y ∈ E` for every
`y ∈ H` having some nonzero multiple in `E`. -/]
theorem Subgroup.FG.exists_pow_mem_of_mem_of_pow_mem {G : Type*} [CommGroup G] {H : Subgroup G}
    (hH : H.FG) (E : Subgroup G) :
    ∃ u ≠ 0, ∀ y ∈ H, ∀ a ≠ 0, y ^ a ∈ E → y ^ u ∈ E := by
  have : Group.FG H := (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg H).mpr hH
  have := TauCeti.CommGroup.finite_torsion_of_fg (H ⧸ E.subgroupOf H)
  refine ⟨Monoid.exponent (CommGroup.torsion (H ⧸ E.subgroupOf H)),
    Monoid.exponent_ne_zero_of_finite, fun y hy a ha hya => ?_⟩
  -- the class of `y` in `H ⧸ (E ⊓ H)` is torsion, so the exponent of the torsion kills it
  have hq : IsOfFinOrder (QuotientGroup.mk (s := E.subgroupOf H) ⟨y, hy⟩) :=
    isOfFinOrder_iff_pow_eq_one.mpr ⟨a, Nat.pos_of_ne_zero ha, by
      rwa [← QuotientGroup.mk_pow, QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff, Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf]⟩
  have hu := congrArg Subtype.val
    (Monoid.pow_exponent_eq_one (⟨_, hq⟩ : CommGroup.torsion (H ⧸ E.subgroupOf H)))
  rwa [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, OneMemClass.coe_one, ← QuotientGroup.mk_pow,
    QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff, Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf] at hu

end
